emscripten 5.0.1 (as installed by emsdk) — cwrap's fast path: accept 'bigint'
args, and agree with ccall on a boolean return.

PROPOSAL, NOT APPLIED LOCALLY. picovoxel works around this by binding the raw
exports directly instead of using cwrap; this file is the fix shaped as a diff
for emscripten-core/emscripten. Ledger row U16.

Defect 1 (src/lib/libccall.js:148). `numericArgs` accepts only 'number' and
'boolean', so a single 'bigint' argument demotes the whole binding from the
fast path (the raw export) to `ccall` — string-keyed `getCFunc` re-resolution, a
per-argument converter loop, and stack save/restore on every call. A BigInt
needs no marshalling at all under -sWASM_BIGINT, which is default-on
(src/settings.js:1475): ccall's own `toC` table has no 'bigint' entry, so the
value already falls through unconverted. The fix is one term.

Defect 2 (same block, vs :59). `numericRet` is `returnType !== 'string'`, so a
boolean-returning export with numeric args takes the fast path and returns the
raw i32, while the identical `ccall` returns `Boolean(ret)` via
`convertReturnValue`. cwrap and ccall disagree on one signature. Fixed here by
coercing in the fast path rather than by dropping to ccall, so the perf property
the fast path exists for is kept.

Not changed, deliberately: the whole block is `#if !ASSERTIONS`, so debug builds
marshal every call through ccall and get different per-call semantics from
release builds. That is a policy question for maintainers, not a two-token fix.

Measured motivation (picovoxel WebAssembly port, emsdk 5.0.1): 143 of 147
PicoGK exports take a handle argument and were therefore all on the slow path;
`Lattice_AddBeam` 154.3 ns via cwrap->ccall vs 56.4 ns calling the export
directly, `Voxels_bIsEmpty` 99.4 -> 34.7 ns — a 2.7-2.9x per-call tax on a
binding that needed no conversion. Evidence:
bench/results/webgpu-v2/SK-0.2.md.

Target file sha256 (emscripten-version.txt = 5.0.1):
0cad844a39bb1f8dcc0e0fa361b09cc956334ba73635b244db32dc11ba33b260  src/lib/libccall.js

Applies with `patch -p1` at the root of the emscripten checkout.

--- a/src/lib/libccall.js
+++ b/src/lib/libccall.js
@@ -145,10 +145,14 @@
 #if !ASSERTIONS
     // When the function takes numbers and returns a number, we can just return
     // the original function
-    var numericArgs = !argTypes || argTypes.every((type) => type === 'number' || type === 'boolean');
+    var numericArgs = !argTypes || argTypes.every((type) => type === 'number' || type === 'boolean' || type === 'bigint');
     var numericRet = returnType !== 'string';
     if (numericRet && numericArgs && !opts) {
-      return getCFunc(ident);
+      var func = getCFunc(ident);
+      // ccall coerces a boolean return value (convertReturnValue, above). The
+      // fast path must agree, or cwrap and ccall return different things for
+      // the same signature: a raw i32 here, `true`/`false` there.
+      return returnType === 'boolean' ? (...args) => Boolean(func(...args)) : func;
     }
 #endif
     return (...args) => ccall(ident, returnType, argTypes, args, opts);
